.TH UPDATE-NODE-ALTERNATIVES 8 "2026-05-09" "update-node-alternatives 0.4" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
update-node-alternatives \- manage system-wide Node.js versions via NVM and update-alternatives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B update-node-alternatives
.RI [ options ]
.I action
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B update-node-alternatives
manages multiple Node.js versions installed system-wide. It combines the
.BR nvm (1)
infrastructure (to download and store Node.js binaries under
.IR /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/ )
with Debian's
.BR update-alternatives (1)
mechanism (to switch the
.IR /usr/local/bin/node ,
.IR npm ,
.IR npx
and
.IR corepack
symlinks).
.PP
It is designed in the spirit of
.BR update-java-alternatives (8)
and honours the
.B DEBIAN_FRONTEND
convention (see
.BR debconf (7)).
The interactive frontend is selected automatically:
.BR zenity (1)
or
.BR kdialog (1)
when a graphical session is detected
.RB ( \%$DISPLAY
or
.BR \%$WAYLAND_DISPLAY ),
.BR whiptail (1)
or
.BR dialog (1)
on a TTY, with a plain readline fallback. The choice can be forced with
.B \-\-frontend
or via the
.B DEBIAN_FRONTEND
environment variable.
.PP
Priority for
.BR update-alternatives (1)
is computed from the Node.js version: \fImajor * 1000000 + minor * 1000 + patch\fR (e.g. v22.14.0 \[->] 22014000).
When running in
.B auto
mode, the highest priority version wins.
.PP
.B Slaves are discovered dynamically.
On every
.BR \-\-install ", " \-\-set ", " \-\-auto " or " \-\-update ,
the contents of
.IR /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/<version>/bin/
are scanned and every executable other than
.B node
is registered as a slave alternative. Binaries installed system-wide
through
.B sudo npm install -g
.RB ( ng ", " tsc ", " pnpm ", ...)
therefore become
.IR /usr/local/bin/<name>
symlinks managed by
.BR update-alternatives (1)
without any change to the script.
.SS Per-user override
.B /etc/profile.d/update-node-alternatives.sh
exports
.B NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX=$HOME/.npm-global
(unless the user already configured one) and prefixes
.B $NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX/bin
to
.BR PATH .
A regular user can then run
.B npm install -g <pkg>
without
.BR sudo (8)
to override the system-wide binary; PATH order alone arbitrates which
copy wins, no custom logic in the wrapper.
.SH ACTIONS
Exactly one action must be provided.
.SS NVM actions
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-install " " \fIversion\fR
Download the requested Node.js version through NVM and register it with
.BR update-alternatives (1).
.I version
may be a number
.RI ( 22 ),
a full version
.RI ( v22.14.0 )
or an alias
.RI ( lts/jod ", " lts/* ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remove " " \fIversion\fR
Remove an installed Node.js version. Deregisters it from
.BR update-alternatives (1)
and asks NVM to delete the files. Prompts for confirmation if the version
is currently active.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-list\-remote " [" \-\-lts ]
List versions available for download. With
.B \-\-lts
only Long Term Support releases are shown.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-list\-packages " " \fIversion\fR
List npm global packages installed for
.IR version
(read from the
.I lib/node_modules
directory of that version).
.BR npm
and
.BR corepack
are excluded from the list.
.TP
.BR \-\-upgrade " " \fIversion\fR " [" \-\-from " " \fIprevious\fR ]
Install
.IR version ,
make it the active alternative and offer to migrate the previously installed
global packages onto it. If
.B \-\-from
is omitted the currently active version is used as source.
.TP
.BR \-\-reinstall\-packages " " \-\-from " " \fIsrc\fR " " \-\-to " " \fIdst\fR
Migrate global npm packages from
.I src
to
.I dst
without installing a new Node.js version. Both versions must already be
installed locally.
.TP
.BR \-\-install\-packages " [" \-\-to " " \fIversion\fR ]
Collect the global npm packages of every other installed Node.js version,
grouped by name (each entry lists the package versions found and the
Node.js version holding them), and offer to install a selection into
.I version
(default: the active version). Packages already present in the target
start unchecked. The newly installed binaries are then registered as
alternatives, as with
.BR \-\-update .
.PP
.B Compatibility check.
Whenever packages are offered for a target version (this action,
.BR \-\-set ,
.B \-\-upgrade
and
.BR \-\-reinstall\-packages ),
the
.I engines.node
range of each package is evaluated against the target with the semver
module bundled with that version's npm. Incompatible packages start
unchecked and are flagged; packages declaring no range are flagged as
unchecked. Packages are reinstalled, never copied, with the target's npm
running under the target's node and with
.BR \-\-engine\-strict ,
so native modules are rebuilt for its ABI and npm refuses a registry
release whose range excludes the target. Each package is installed
separately: one failure does not block the others, and the exit status
is non-zero if any failed.
.SS update-alternatives actions
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List the Node.js versions installed under
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/
together with their computed priority and the current alternative.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-set " " \fInodename\fR
Switch the node alternative to
.I nodename
(exact directory name, e.g.
.IR v22.14.0 )
in manual mode. When the active version changes, a checklist is shown to
migrate the previous version's global packages.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Re-register every installed Node.js version with
.BR update-alternatives (1),
re-scanning
.IR <version>/bin/
to pick up new slaves. Useful after manually copying a version into
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/
or after a
.B sudo npm install -g
that produced a binary you want exposed under
.IR /usr/local/bin/ .
There is no automatic post-\fBnpm\fR hook by design; this is the
explicit re-sync entry point.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-auto
Switch the node alternative back to automatic mode (highest priority wins).
.SS Per-user globals
.TP
.B \-\-promote\-user\-globals
Run as root via
.BR sudo (8)
(the script refuses without
.BR \%$SUDO_USER ).
Discovers the npm
.I prefix
of the invoking user via
.B sudo -u $SUDO_USER -H npm config get prefix
(falling back to
.IR \%~/.npm-global ),
lists every per-user
.B npm install -g
package not already covered system-wide at >= the per-user version,
shows an interactive checklist, then re-installs the selected packages
in the system-wide layer. The system-wide install runs with
.B HOME=/root
so that the user's
.I .npmrc
(registry, authentication tokens, ...) is never reused for the root
install. Calls
.BR \-\-update
at the end so the freshly installed binaries become alternatives.
Optionally chains into
.B \-\-cleanup\-user\-globals
under the original user via
.BR \%"exec\ sudo\ -u\ $SUDO_USER" .
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup\-user\-globals
Run as a regular user (refuses if invoked as root). Lists every
per-user
.B npm install -g
package for which the system-wide layer currently provides a >= version
and offers to remove the redundant per-user copies via
.BR "npm uninstall -g" .
Idempotent: a package whose per-user version is newer or which has no
system-wide counterpart is never offered for removal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Be verbose about what is happening.
.TP
.BR \-\-frontend " " \fIname\fR
Force a specific interactive frontend. Valid values:
.BR dialog " (whiptail/dialog), "
.BR readline ", "
.BR gnome " (zenity), "
.BR kde " (kdialog), and "
.BR noninteractive .
Overrides
.BR \%$DEBIAN_FRONTEND .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dialog
Alias for
.BR \-\-frontend " " readline.
Useful over SSH sessions without TTY colour support or in scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-lts
When combined with
.BR \-\-list\-remote ,
only show Long Term Support releases.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, missing privileges, unknown version, NVM or
.BR update-alternatives (1)
failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/
System-wide NVM installation (created by the script on first run, or by
.B make install
when installing from source).
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/nvm.sh
NVM shell library sourced by the script.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/
Installed Node.js versions (one directory per version).
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node_binaries.info
State file listing binaries currently registered as alternatives.
The first line
.RB ( "Binaries=node\ npm\ npx\ ..." )
is the union across every installed version (read at startup to know
which alternatives to remove on re-register, and consumed by
.IR postrm
on
.B apt purge
to drop every dynamic slave). Subsequent
.B Binaries.<version>=...
lines record the slaves of each individual version for diagnostics.
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/update-node-alternatives.sh
POSIX-sh snippet sourced on login: defaults
.B NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX
to
.IR \%~/.npm-global
and prefixes
.B $NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX/bin
to
.BR PATH .
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/update-node-alternatives
.BR bash (1)
completion script (installed verbatim under
.I $(PREFIX)/share/bash-completion/completions/
when building from source).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/node
.TQ
.I /usr/local/bin/npm
.TQ
.I /usr/local/bin/npx
.TQ
.I /usr/local/bin/corepack
Symlinks managed by
.BR update-alternatives (1)
(node is the master, the rest are slaves).
.SH PRIVILEGES
.BR \-\-list ", " \-\-list\-remote ", " \-\-list\-packages " and "
.B \-\-cleanup\-user\-globals
must be run as a regular user (the cleanup action explicitly refuses
when invoked as root). Every other action modifies system state (NVM
store or
.BR update-alternatives (1)
database) and must be run as root, typically via
.BR sudo (8).
.B \-\-promote\-user\-globals
additionally requires
.B \%$SUDO_USER
to be set so that the source per-user npm prefix can be discovered.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the latest Node.js 22 and register it:
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-install 22
.RE
.PP
List available LTS releases:
.PP
.RS 4
update-node-alternatives \-\-list\-remote \-\-lts
.RE
.PP
Upgrade from v20.18.1 to the latest v22, migrating global packages:
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-upgrade 22 \-\-from v20.18.1
.RE
.PP
Install into the active version some global packages found in the other
versions, after the engines.node check:
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-install\-packages
.RE
.PP
Switch the active version without touching anything else:
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-set v22.14.0
.RE
.PP
Return to automatic mode (highest priority wins):
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-auto
.RE
.PP
After a system-wide
.BR "npm install -g" ,
expose the freshly installed binaries under
.IR /usr/local/bin/ :
.PP
.RS 4
sudo npm install -g @angular/cli
.br
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-update
.RE
.PP
Promote a user's per-user
.BR "npm install -g"
packages into the system-wide layer (and offer to clean up the per-user
copies right after):
.PP
.RS 4
sudo update-node-alternatives \-\-promote\-user\-globals
.RE
.PP
Drop per-user
.BR "npm install -g"
packages that the system-wide layer already covers at the same or a
newer version:
.PP
.RS 4
update-node-alternatives \-\-cleanup\-user\-globals
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEBIAN_FRONTEND
When set to
.BR dialog ", " readline ", " gnome ", " kde
or
.BR noninteractive ,
selects the interactive frontend. Other values fall back to auto-detection.
Under
.BR noninteractive ,
.B \-\-promote\-user\-globals
and
.B \-\-cleanup\-user\-globals
print a candidate report and exit without modifying anything.
.TP
.B NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX
Read by
.BR npm (1)
to determine the install root for
.BR "npm install -g" .
The shipped
.I /etc/profile.d/update-node-alternatives.sh
sets it to
.IR \%~/.npm-global
unless the user already configured one.
.TP
.B SUDO_USER
Required by
.BR \-\-promote\-user\-globals
to identify which user's npm globals to promote.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update-alternatives (1),
.BR update-java-alternatives (8),
.BR debconf (7),
.BR nvm (1),
.BR whiptail (1),
.BR dialog (1),
.BR zenity (1),
.BR kdialog (1),
.BR npm (1)
